      "delta": "Inject caller-owned line-process spawn; pass explicit env unchanged; preserve server ids and support replies; default/per-request timeouts; bounded held and pending state with fatal overflow; release timers on settlement, failed write, exit and kill. S2b: settlement consumer errors reject already-dequeued waiters; no uncaught timer failure. Re-vendor: omit upstream home queue and executable diagnostics; preserve direct injected ownership and bounded exitError; retain handled spawned promise. Native replies await acknowledged stdin writes under bounded ownership. 0.33.1 re-vendor: MCP credential redaction of error and exit text through the caller-owned exitError."
